bin/
.claude/*
# …except the project skills, which are documentation for working on this repo
# and should travel with a clone. `.claude/*` (not `.claude/`) is what makes the
# negation possible: git cannot re-include anything under an ignored directory,
# only under an ignored glob. settings.local.json and the rest stay ignored.
!.claude/skills/

# This repo's own prompt backlog, written by the tool it builds. A project
# backlog is committed with the repo in a normal project (see README); here it
# is just dogfooding scratch and does not belong in the history. The whole
# directory, not just todos.json: attachments land in .cats-todo/images, and
# ignoring only the manifest left the screenshots showing up as untracked.
.cats-todo/

# The compiled manager, when it is built in place rather than into bin/. `go
# build` with no -o drops it here named after the module, and a stray 10 MB
# binary showing up as untracked is noise on every status.
/cats-todo
